# Site design system — primitives + token rules

The public site shares **one** design-system grammar. Use the primitives in
`src/components/ui/`. Do not invent sibling components or paste raw class
strings.

Pre-read [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-16-design-uplift.md`](../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-16-design-uplift.md)
for the audit that produced these primitives.

## Primitives (import from `@/components/ui/...`)

| Primitive | When | Don't |
|---|---|---|
| `<Card variant="default">` | default surface — articles, form blocks, empty sections | raw `<div className="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white shadow-sm">` |
| `<Card variant="elevated" interactive>` | clickable nav tile / path / channel — adds hover-lift + brand accent border + focus parity + motion-reduce fallback | raw `<div className="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 …hover:-translate-y-1…">` |
| `<Card variant="outline">` | the historical `border-l-2 border-opseu-blue/30 pl-5` ridge used by captions, complaint-vs-grievance, pre-disciplinary-log | raw `<li className="min-w-0 border-l-2 border-opseu-blue/30 pl-5">` |
| `<Card variant="ghost">` | soft brand-tinted band (Catalyst hubs, demo bands, regional nav) | raw `<div className="rounded-xl border border-opseu-blue/15 bg-opseu-blue/[0.04]">` |
| `<Eyebrow tone="brand\|amber\|muted\|danger\|success">` | tracked uppercase micro-label | raw `<p className="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">`; raw `<p className="text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em]">` |
| `<SectionHeading id eyebrow title intro align as>` | in-section heading block with eyebrow → h2 → constrained intro; `scroll-mt-28` baked in | rebuild the eyebrow+h2+intro stack inline; hand-roll `<section className="scroll-mt-28">` blocks |
| `<IconChip tone size>` | round square hosting an inline SVG affordance | raw `<span className="inline-flex h-10 w-10 … rounded-lg bg-opseu-blue/10">` |
| `<ButtonLink variant="primary\|outline\|ghost" size="md\|sm\|lg" block trailingArrow>` | navigation CTA styled as a button | raw `<a className="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-opseu-blue px-5 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white …">` |
| `<Button>` | form submit, in-page interaction | don't wrap `<Button>` inside `<Link>` — use `<ButtonLink>` |

## Typography tokens (import from `@/lib/constants/public-type`)

- `PUBLIC_PAGE_TITLE_CLASS` — page h1. Already used by home, captions,
  examples, install, manifesto, support, guides, tools.
- `PUBLIC_SECTION_TITLE_CLASS` — h2 inside `<SectionHeading>`.
- `PUBLIC_CARD_TITLE_CLASS` — h3 on a card face.

Never re-roll these as inline clamps (`text-[clamp(…)]`). If a size is wrong
for your context, fix it in `public-type.ts` and the cascade updates all
chapters.

## Color tokens — banned/required

| Role | Use | Never |
|---|---|---|
| Body copy (public pages) | `text-slate-700` | `text-gray-700/800/900`, `text-black` |
| Body copy variant | `text-slate-600` | `text-gray-500/600` |
| Heading chrome | `text-opseu-dark` (existing) | `text-black` |
| Brand CTA | `bg-opseu-blue` (existing) | `bg-orange-*`, `bg-red-*` |
| Brand CTA hover | `bg-opseu-dark` (existing) | re-define hover state |
| Card surface | `bg-white` | `bg-gray-50` for default surface |

Exceptions ("always OK"):
- `text-gray-500` is allowed **only** on `<Eyebrow tone="muted">` (eyebrow
  chrome) and on `disabled` chips.
- `text-amber-700/800/900` for amber-tone eyebrows, hint callouts,
  labour-playbook bands.
- `text-red-*` for danger/destructive banners only.

## Layout / card grid rules

- Cards in a grid: `gap-4 sm:gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3` (or the
  variant you need) **must** match the dataset count. Don't ship
  `grid-cols-3` with two children.
- Channel / Comms tiles: `gap-4 sm:gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4`.
- Path tile cluster: `gap-5 sm:gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`.
- Pin the CTA to the bottom of the card with `mt-auto pt-2` inside the
  Card, **not** the grid parent.
- Internal anchors get `scroll-mt-28` (the global header height). `<SectionHeading>`
  bakes it in; otherwise apply manually on `<section id>`.

## Anti-patterns — do not ship

1. `border-l-2 border-opseu-blue/30 pl-5` as a raw `<li>` chrome — use
   `<Card variant="outline">` or `<GuideCatalogCard>`.
2. `rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white` flat without `shadow-sm`
   — that is **sub-elevation** and reads as unfinished. Use
   `<Card variant="default">` instead.
3. `inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-opseu-blue …`
   raw `<a>` for a CTA — use `<ButtonLink variant="primary">`.
4. Inline uppercase `text-gray-500` eyebrow labels — use `<Eyebrow>`.
5. `not-first-of-type:mt-0` margin-doubling hack — fold into the parent
   `space-y-N` + drop the section's own self-margin instead.
6. Hand-rolling a hover-lift surface outside `<Card variant="elevated">`.
7. New CTA class strings — extend `guideCtaClasses.ts` or use
   `<ButtonLink>`. Do not invent a 7th dialect.

## When introducing a new pattern

Add it to the **table at the top of this file** before merging. Prefer
extending an existing primitive (a new `variant`, `tone`, or `size`) before
authoring a sibling component. The audit at
`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-16-design-uplift.md` §2 tracks the
inventory; if your new primitive appears there as a "still inline" item,
prefer fixing that line instead of duplicating.

## Locale tokens (do not rename)

`--opseu-blue` and `--opseu-dark` are CSS variables set in
`src/app/globals.css` as **brand orange / brand dark** (orange `#c2410c`)
despite the legacy name. **Never** rename them within one PR — the canvas
capture pipeline, the homepage hero gradient, and the per-tenant Brand Kit
all read these variables. Existing literal references to
`text-opseu-blue`/`bg-opseu-blue`/`hover:bg-opseu-dark` are intentional and
must continue to map to the orange brand color.
